{
 "priority": 7,
 "source_bins": [
  "talk.bin"
 ],
 "strings": {
  "You know I'm always down for a competition.": "",
  "I expected as much. Then let's get started.": "",
  "Yeah! I won!": "",
  "Aww! Can't believe I lost!": "",
  "Your aim is way too good, Yagami-san!": "",
  "Oh, it's a draw?": "",
  "Oooh, I was so close too!": "",
  "I guess we'll find out the true winner next time.": "",
  "Dang!": "",
  "You're much better than I thought, Nanami-san.": "",
  "Hehehe. Told you I was good.": "",
  "Sorry to make you wait, Takayuki-san.": "",
  "Do you feel better now?": "",
  "If I say no, will you let me slap you again?": "",
  "Huh? Are you seriously still upset?": "",
  "Haha, I was just teasing. You know, like you always do.": "",
  "Ahaha. You know me too well.": "",
  "Were you waiting long, Takayuki-san?": "",
  "Nope, not at all.": "",
  "Oh, that's good.": "",
  "(Oh yeah. Maybe I should give Nanami a present?)": "",
  "I actually bought a little something for you.": "",
  "Mhm. Here, check it out.": "",
  "Wow, a wristwatch? This is actually pretty cute!": "",
  "I love it! The smartwatch is handy, but this one's way cuter.": "",
  "I know you use a smartwatch, but I thought if you ever want to change things up...": "",
  "I'm gonna try it on.": "",
  "Sure. Please do.": "",
  "Looks good. I think it really fits you, Nanami.": "",
  "Hehehe. How's it look?": "",
  "Takayuki-san, you have good taste!": "",
  "Here you go, Nanami.": "",
  "Oh! Oh my gosh. How expensive was this?": "",
  "Expensive enough to show you how much I care.": "",
  "Haha, well. It's a little heavy, but I'm happy anyway. Thanks.": "",
  "Feel free to use it as much as you like.": "",
  "(Maybe she was a tad uncomfortable with the price.)": "",
  "I got a present for you, Nanami. I think it'll look good on you.": "",
  "Really? Are you sure?": "",
  "Yeah. I don't know if you'll like it or not, though.": "",
  "I... I do! Uh, thanks!": "",
  "Huh? Is it not really your style?": "",
  "Hmm, not exactly. It's... how would I put it... a bit too flashy?": "",
  "Ah... I can see that.": "",
  "But maybe it'll look better once I try it on.": "",
  "True. I'm sure you'll make it look good.": "",
  "Thanks, Takayuki-san.": "",
  "(Looks like she wasn't too fond of it.)": "",
  "Hey, it's cute! Thanks, Takayuki-san!": "",
  "(I'm glad she's happy with it.)": "",
  "Any ideas where to go?": "",
  "(Hmm, what's a fun thing we could do...)": "",
  "Sounds good! Then I'll cheer you on with everything I've got!": "",
  "Thanks for today, Takayuki! I had a lot of fun!": "",
  "Same here.": "",
  "Let's go out again sometime, okay?": "",
  "(Nanami always knows exactly how to cheer me up.)": "",
  "Ready to race your heart out?": "",
  "(Nanami's watching, so... I can't afford to lose!)": "",
  "All right! I got first place!": "",
  "The way you flew was amazing, Takayuki-san!": "",
  "Guess all my practice paid off.": "",
  "Damn, that was a total crash and burn...": "",
  "Aww, I totally thought you could pull it off, too.": "",
  "(Next time for sure...)": "",
  "I'm... a failure...": "",
  "Don't beat yourself up too hard. I mean, maybe you were distracted or something.": "",
  "(Damn. That was really lame.)": "",
  "Wow, great job, Takayuki-san!": "",
  "Maybe I should stop being a detective and pick up baseball full-time.": "",
  "Haha, don't get too ahead of yourself now.": "",
  "(I'm glad she saw me at my best today.)": "",
  "Hmm, I thought I'd get a higher score. Guess it is what it is.": "",
  "Hey, there's always next time!": "",
  "Ugh, I completely sucked out there...": "",
  "(God, that was terrible.)": "",
  "Let's play each other, Nanami.": "",
  "Sure. Don't expect me to lose, though.": "",
  "Oh, don't worry. I'll be taking this seriously.": "",
  "All right then, show me what you got!": "",
  "Boom! I was right on target today!": "",
  "Noooo! I lost! Ahhh, I can't believe it!": "",
  "I'll make sure this doesn't happen a next time!": "",
  "Hey, I'm always up for a challenge.": "",
  "It was a draw...": "",
  "Yeah, but it was a pretty good match, right?": "",
  "It sure was. Let's definitely do this again.": "",
  "All right! Beat you fair and square, Takayuki-san!": "",
  "Dang! You sure did.": "",
  "Don't worry, I'm always up for a rematch.": "",
  "Good, 'cause I don't plan on losing next time.": "",
  "Hey, I'm the one who dragged you out, so what's up with the gift?": "",
  "My pleasure, Yagami-san. You're looking handsome as ever.": "",
  "Well... I'm not sure. I mean, I do get along with her pretty well...": "",
  "Stop being so vague! Nothing good will happen if you keep thinking indecisive like that!": "",
  "...You might have a point there.": "",
  "Oh, of course.": "",
  "Ohhhh! Hey, how about this!?": "",
  "(Is this really the right thing to do...?)": "",
  "Well of course not... Unfortunately, I think this is the only way to get to her.": "",
  "Hmm. I'm not so sure...": "",
  "All right, Yukko. She agreed to go with me.": "",
  "I knew she would, especially if it was an infidelity case.": "",
  "So where should we hold the investigation?": "",
  "Well, we're pretending to be a couple... so somewhere a couple might go.": "",
  "Like somewhere with a lot of love hotels?": "",
  "That... does seem plausible.": "",
  "Let's make it the Hotel District then! I'll be wandering around there, so make sure to follow me!": "",
  "Uh-huh. Yeah. So it looks like our target's in the Hotel District. Yup. I'll be counting on you.": "",
  "(Hope this doesn't end in total disaster...)": "",
  "Huh? You're not gonna participate?": "",
  "Oh, I am. I was just getting mentally prepared.": "",
  "(Okay, time to select the course.)": "",
  "Oh, I still am. I was just... I dunno.": "",
  "Today, it's gonna be one home run after another!": "",
  "You seem pretty pumped.": "",
  "I sure am! Don't disappoint me now!": "",
  "Hehe, I decided to change things up a bit. So, what do you think?": "",
  "I... don't normally wear them around guys.": "",
  "So that means you've gotten more comfortable around me?": "",
  "...Let's just say today's special!": "",
  "Sure! I could use some exercise myself.": "",
  "Ooh, I love a good challenge!": "",
  "I'm warning you though, I won't be easy!": "",
  "(I need to get in touch with Yukko-san.)": "",
  "Nothing. Not even an angry emoji.": "",
  "She hasn't responded to me either.": "",
  "I guess we'll just have to be patient.": "",
  "(Oh, that's right. Maybe I should give Nanami-san a present?)": "",
  "I actually bought something for you, Nanami-san.": "",
  "Yep. Check this out.": "",
  "Oh, how cute! Is that a wristwatch?": "",
  "(Whew. I guess she likes it.)": "",
  "I'll keep it close!": "",
  "Hehehe. So, how's it look?": "",
  "I think it fits your style perfectly.": "",
  "It sure does! Yagami-san, you really have good taste!": "",
  "Here's a little something for you, Nanami-san.": "",
  "Wow, is this really okay? I mean, how expensive was this?": "",
  "Haha, okay then. Well... it's a little heavy, but I'm happy with it anyway. Thanks.": "",
  "Nanami-san, here's something I thought would look good on you.": "",
  "...O-Oh! This is... neat?": "",
  "Not exactly. It's... I don't know, flashy?": "",
  "Aww, it's adorable! Thanks, Yagami-san!": "",
  "(Oh, should I buy a present for Nanami-san beforehand?)": "",
  "(I bet Le Marche would have some good stuff.)": "",
  "Of course not! You're different from everyone else.": "",
  "Yeah. You can eat things other than dessert and still live, right?": "",
  "What do you think? Do I look like I could be your girlfriend?": "",
  "That's perfect! It looks great on you.": "",
  "Yay! I'm glad I spent all that time getting dressed up.": "",
  "It's great! I knew it'd look good on you. I think it looks even better seeing it in person.": "",
  "Hehe. I thought it looked good, too. Thank you so much, Takayuki-san!": "",
  "I actually bought something for you, Nanami.": "",
  "Huh? Really? You got me a present?": "",
  "Yeah. I hope you like it.": "",
  "A jacket?": "",
  "Well, if you don't like it you can just pawn it down at Ebisu.": "",
  "Hey, I would never sell something you gave me. This is totally my style, too!": "",
  "Well, I'm just glad you like it.": "",
  "Yeah. Here.": "",
  "Wow, thank you! You have good taste, Yagami-san.": "",
  "Buying clothes for a woman isn't easy, but this is totally my style.": "",
  "Heh. Not a problem for someone with a detective's power of observation.": "",
  "Don't get too ahead of yourself, Sherlock.": "",
  "Excuse me, but do you have a minute?": "",
  "Let me introduce myself. My name is Shin Fujimori.": "",
  "Have you ever thought about investing, sir?": "",
  "Honestly, I think you're better off talking about that sort of thing with someone who actually has money.": "",
  "Er, well, I say \"investment\" but nowadays anyone can do it as long as they have a smartphone!": "",
  "You can invest on your phone?": "",
  "Of course. Ever heard of crowdfunding? It's where you gather online donations from all over the world...": "",
  "It's become a big trend in the past few years.": "",
  "And to streamline this process, we developed an app called Quickstarter.": "",
  "You can invest however much money you want, to whomever you wish, whenever you like! All from the comfort of your phone!": "",
  "Well, it sounds easy enough... But the hard part, you know, is actually having money.": "",
  "Indeed. That's why millions of people make micro-investments with Quickstarter. Only a small donation is needed.": "",
  "And even small donations make a big difference. They all add up to help a campaign reach various milestones.": "",
  "Finally, once a campaign meets its goal, everyone who invested gains priority benefits.": "",
  "Priority benefits? Can you give me an example?": "",
  "Let's see. For starters, you can get special products shipped to you, or you'll gain access to brand-new facilities!": "",
  "Hmm... That actually sounds pretty neat.": "",
  "Doesn't it?": "",
  "I'll tell you this much. I once started up a company of my own, but I had a hard time raising the necessary funds...": "",
  "And wouldn't you know it, I got everything I needed from a crowdfunding platform I signed up with overseas.": "",
  "That's why I created this app, to help other entrepreneurs worldwide.": "",
  "Wow, so you're the president of a company?": "",
  "Oh, it's quite small, so it's not really a big deal.": "",
  "Anyway, the point of my story is: please try using Quickstarter for yourself sometime!": "",
  "Okay. I'll at least install it for the time being.": "",
  "Please do! And by all means, let me know how it goes!": "",
  "Hey there! Excuse me, sir!": "",
  "Oh, Fujimori-san. You can call me Yagami, by the way.": "",
  "Yagami-san, then. Has Quickstarter been useful to you?": "",
  "Oh yeah. It's especially nice to see the campaign you've invested in finally reach its goal.": "",
  "Exactly!": "",
  "A lot of people out there are full of amazing ideas, but since they're low on funding, they can't make them happen.": "",
  "But with a single app, they can gather funds more easily, which gives them a greater opportunity to succeed.": "",
  "Also, it helps people experiment with their creativity, which is sorely lacking in many of the larger companies.": "",
  "And personally, I believe that putting innovators in touch with investors can help make the world a better place.": "",
  "I respect that. It's good to help people accomplish their dreams.": "",
  "All I'm really doing is returning the favor that crowdfunding helped me achieve.": "",
  "What goes around comes around, huh?": "",
  "Oh, that's right! I had this great idea I wanted to share with everyone.": "",
  "So I started up a Quickstarter campaign of my own!": "",
  "Please consider a donation if you feel like helping out.": "",
  "Is that right? Then I'll definitely check it out sometime.": "",
  "I appreciate that. Not just your time, but also your consideration. May we meet again on the road to success!": "",
  "Hello there, Tomioka-san. Uh... nice weather today?": "",
  "Ah, perfect timing, Yagami-kun!": "",
  "Why, what's going on?": "",
  "Well, I managed to lose the keys to the building's roller shutter... and now I can't get inside.": "",
  "Seriously? That's unfortunate.": "",
  "It is. I'm really not sure what to do...": "",
  "Well, you'll have to get it open somehow.": "",
  "It doesn't take a detective to figure that out. Now will you help me get this lock open?": "",
  "I'm sure you can do it. It'll be just like a crime drama! All you need's a knife and a roll of duct tape!": "",
  "I doubt it's actually that simple. And what show are you referencing, anyway?": "",
  "It doesn't matter! Now can't you at least try something?": "",
  "(I didn't know Tomioka-san could be so demanding... I'd better get this open, and quick.)": "",
  "All right, it's open.": "",
  "I knew you could do it! Thanks a bunch, Yagami-kun.": "",
  "Sure, no problem. Well then, I'll be off now...": "",
  "Aren't you forgetting something? *cough cough* Something along the lines of <font_kind=yakuza_italic>three months' rent</font_kind>?": "",
  "Y-You know, the... One thing I should... Would you mind waiting a little longer?": "",
  "...Good grief. I'm not running a youth hostel here. Did you know buildings actually cost <font_kind=yakuza_italic>money</font_kind> to maintain? Amazing, I know.": "",
  "Actually... that gives me an idea!": "",
  "...Should I be afraid to ask?": "",
  "You're an able-bodied young man, and you seem to be good at opening locks. Why don't I introduce you to a locksmith I know?": "",
  "What for?": "",
  "I was thinking you could take a part-time job there. You know, to earn some extra money. Like the kind you owe me.": "",
  "Aww, do I have to...?": "",
  "You sure do. In fact, I'm calling him right now. Gotta strike while the iron's hot! ": "",
  "H-Hey... Hold the phone...": "",
  "...Hello, Koizuka-kun? Sorry for the sudden call. You see, there's this tenant who lives in my building...": "",
  "Tomioka-san, what a pleasure it is to see you. Is he the one you told me about?": "",
  "Yep, this here's Yagami-kun.": "",
  "Who's that, Tomioka-san?": "",
  "You're looking at Toshiro Koizuka, one of the finest locksmiths in Kamurocho. But I just call him Koizuka-kun.": "",
  "Good to meet you, Yagami-san.": "",
  "...The pleasure's all mine.": "",
  "Now then, Yagami-kun. Work hard to earn your keep.": "",
  "And regarding the details of our arrangement, just ask Koizuka-kun. Hope he doesn't work you to the bone!": "",
  "(Seriously, Tomioka-san? I know I'm a failure when it comes to paying rent, but... Hmm. I guess that's why this happened.)": "",
  "Mind if I start explaining how things work around here?": "",
  "N-Not at all.": "",
  "Whenever we get a job request, I'll pass it on to you. Then you'll head over to the client's place and open the lock in question.": "",
  "That's all there is to it. You <font_kind=yakuza_italic>can</font_kind> open locks, right?": "",
  "Y-Yeah.": "",
  "Good. I'm in my shop most hours, so come by when you're ready to get to work.": ""
 },
 "ref_tm": {
  "Nope, not at all.": "ไม่เลยครับ ไม่เข้าใจเลย",
  "Oh, that's good.": "อ้อ ดีเลย",
  "Really? Are you sure?": "จริงเหรอ? แน่ใจนะ?",
  "Same here.": "เหมือนกันเลย",
  "Exactly!": "ใช่เลย!",
  "Why, what's going on?": "ทำไมเหรอ มีอะไร?",
  "What for?": "เพื่ออะไรล่ะ?",
  "Y-Yeah.": "อ-อือ"
 }
}
